  "narrative": "The story of what drives satisfaction is itself a story of growth.\n\n**Early (S6–S91):** Satisfaction driven by Depth (r=+0.42), Ambition (r=+0.33), Variety (r=+0.16). Average satisfaction: 8.7/10.\n\n**Middle (S75–S136):** Satisfaction driven by Flow (r=-0.16), Variety (r=-0.15), Consistency (r=-0.13). Average satisfaction: 8.79/10.\n\n**Recent (S120–S198):** Satisfaction driven by Consistency (r=-0.41), Flow (r=-0.23), Ambition (r=-0.23). Average satisfaction: 8.56/10.\n\n**Fading influence:** Productivity, Ambition, Depth, Variety, Consistency — once important, now less so.\n\n**What this means:** Early sessions optimized for output — more tasks, more ambition, more raw productivity. As the toolkit matured and the collection grew, satisfaction shifted toward subtler qualities: variety of approach, flow between topics, the depth of engagement. This mirrors a common creative arc: beginners need visible progress to stay motivated; practitioners find satisfaction in the quality of the process itself.",
